{"assets":["/statement-assets/6182829a0e710e52241acf7d75c7a30b688315fa8969a13c95708b5380e36b62.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"200","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Tractor College"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"While most students still sit their exams, the tractor college has completed the summer exam session. In fact, students study only one subject at this college — the Art of Operating a Tractor. Therefore, at the end of a term a student gets only one mark, a three (satisfactory), a four (good) or a five (excellent). Those who score lower marks are unfortunately expelled."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The college has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" students, and oddly enough, each of them can be on scholarship. The size of the scholarships varies each term. Since the end-of-the-term exam has just ended, it's time to determine the size of the scholarship to the end of next term."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The monthly budget for the scholarships of the Tractor college is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" rubles. To distribute the budget optimally, you must follow these rules:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The students who received the same mark for the exam, should receive the same scholarship;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let us denote the size of the scholarship (in roubles) for students who have received marks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the exam, as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k5"},{"kind":"text","text":", respectively. The values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k5"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be integers and satisfy the inequalities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ k3 ≤ k4 ≤ k5"},{"kind":"text","text":";"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let's assume that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c4"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c5"},{"kind":"text","text":" show how many students received marks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the exam, respectively. The budget of the scholarship should be fully spent on them, that is, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c3·k3 + c4·k4 + c5·k5 = s"},{"kind":"text","text":";"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let's introduce function "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6182829a0e710e52241acf7d75c7a30b688315fa8969a13c95708b5380e36b62.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the value that shows how well the scholarships are distributed between students. In the optimal distribution function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(k3, k4, k5)"},{"kind":"text","text":" takes the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" possible value. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given the results of the exam, and the budget size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", you have to find the optimal distribution of the scholarship."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line has two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 300, 1 ≤ s ≤ 3·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of students and the budget size for the scholarship, respectively. The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, where the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th number represents the mark that the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th student got for the exam. It is guaranteed that at each mark was given to at least one student."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On a single line print three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k5"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the sought values that represent the optimal distribution of the scholarships. If there are multiple optimal answers, print any of them. If there is no answer, print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 11\n3 4 3 5 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 15\n5 3 3 4 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"200E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/200/problem/E"}